 "text": "Hi, how have you been? Generally, you want it dry enough that it' no longer sticky, but not so dry that it starts to chip. Rough estimate is ten minutes for every inch of thickness. Lovely. In that case, I'd start thinking about it now. A basic box with a little bit of detail paint on it is very doable. You can use a clear varnish of some kind, but it'll wash off easily. A light touch with tape is easier than you expect. Rub your fingers across a hidden spot. If they leave no mark, it's dry.",
